  "summary": "The tallest monoliths ever carved in Africa — false-door stelae marking Aksumite royal graves.",
  "description": "Aksum's stela field raises granite monoliths up to 33 metres — the tallest single stones Africans ever quarried, moved and stood — each carved as a miniature palace: false doors at the base, rows of windows and beam-ends climbing the shaft, all in imitation of the multi-storey towers Aksumite elites built. They ringed royal tomb complexes before Christianity arrived with King Ezana; the great stela looted by Mussolini in 1937 came home in 2005. Ethiopian identity, church tradition and archaeological pride all point to this field.",
